// =============================================================================
// quartz.config.ts.template — Quartz site config, rendered to quartz.config.ts
// by quartz/entrypoint.sh at container start.
//
// ONLY the DOMAIN placeholder is substituted (envsubst is given a one-name allow-list), so
// every other dollar sign and backtick-template-looking construct in this
// TypeScript file survives untouched. That restriction is deliberate: a bare
// envsubst over a .ts file would corrupt it.
//
// baseUrl must keep pointing at www.<DOMAIN>/notes — it has to match the path nginx
// proxies (/notes/) or every internal link, the sitemap and the RSS feed point
// at the wrong place.
//
// enableSPA / enablePopovers are off because this site is embedded under a
// path inside another SPA; Quartz's own client-side router would fight with it.
//
// ignorePatterns keeps "private", "templates" and ".obsidian" out of the build
// — the vault is mounted whole, so this list is the only thing stopping
// private notes being published. Check it before adding vault folders.
//
// This file is committed with real content (no secrets). quartz.layout.ts sits
// alongside it and is COPY'd in by quartz/Dockerfile without templating.
// =============================================================================
